  [FAIL] E2 CRITERION (3) -- RAR-CLASS SCATTER.  The candidate's own input, g_ext, spans the width below across the two reconstruction brackets and their 16-84 percentiles; at d log/d log g_ext = -1/2 that is the irreducible scatter of the prediction.  This check passes only if it is inside the 0.1 dex a Kepler-grade law is allowed   (g_ext spread 1.48 dex -> prediction scatter 0.74 dex, against the 0.10 dex criterion; by comparison a 50% Upsilon error moves it only 0.144 dex)

(F) MUTATION CONTROLS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] F1 a_0 x 10 must change the fit: if it does not, the amplitude freedom has eaten the entire a_0 dependence and nothing here measures a_0   (chi2(a_0 x10) = 114.5 vs chi2(a_0) = 102.3, difference +12.1)
  F2 kernel mutation: nu -> 1 in the same quadrature gives M_dyn/M_b = 1.00000000, 1.00000000, 1.00000000, 1.00000000
  [PASS] F2 with the kernel replaced by the identity the monopole law collapses to M_dyn = M_b at every external field, so every number in section A is the kernel and not an artefact of the quadrature   (max |M_dyn/M_b - 1| = 4.86e-11)

========================================================================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================================================================
  Read the checks.  Four things decide this candidate, and none of them favour it:
   (i)   the coefficient it states, nu(e_N), is not the QUMOND monopole coefficient -- that is nu_e(1+L_e/3),
         which is 5/6 nu_e in a deep external field, a 0.079 dex error built into the statement (A2);
   (ii)  the relation closes algebraically from v^4 = G M_b a_0 plus the definition of the EFE radius, so it
         IS A RESTATEMENT of the deep-MOND limit and the external-field effect together (B1), exactly as the
         proposer half-conceded -- and criterion (5) of the hunt says a restatement must be labelled one;
   (iii) it fails criterion (3): its own input g_ext is known to 1.5 dex across the two brackets and their
         percentiles, which at slope -1/2 is 0.74 dex of irreducible scatter against the 0.10 dex allowed (E2);
   (iv)  and on the data it has, the predicted mass saturation is not seen: with a free amplitude per mass bin
         the KiDS-1000 profiles disfavour the truncation by Delta chi2 = +144 (weak field) to +507 (strong
         field), both footings (D1), and the shape alone caps e_N at 6.8e-5, 5.6x below even the no-cluster
         reconstruction median (D2).  BUT THAT EXCLUSION IS NOT ROBUST: allow the neighbours that generate
         g_ext to lens as well and the weak-field truncation is no longer excluded (D5).  So the observational
         verdict is 'excluded at the strong-field bracket, undecided at the weak-field one', not a clean kill.
  The Upsilon lever is -0.815 measured on the amplitude form and +0.445 on r_EFE; but Upsilon is NOT the
  blocker here.  g_ext is, at 5x the size.  Same failure mode as the nine Upsilon items, different quantity.

